' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Zachman classification taxonomy (6x6) vs UAF operational framework (viewpoints).
'   usecase:      Teach taxonomy (Zachman, what slots exist) vs framework (UAF, how to build it).
'   complexity:   variant
'   domain:       enterprise / classification-taxonomy
' ============================================================================
title Example Zachman vs UAF - Taxonomy vs Framework

note as TopNote
  VARIANT:
  Zachman = CLASSIFICATION TAXONOMY. It says WHICH SLOTS exist
  (6 perspectives x 6 interrogatives) but not how to fill them or in what order.
  UAF = OPERATIONAL FRAMEWORK. It says HOW to model a defense
  architecture across viewpoints with relationships/needlines and a process.
  Same enterprise shown both ways below.
end note

' ============ LEFT: ZACHMAN (taxonomy slots) ============
package "ZACHMAN: Designer-What slot" as Z_DW {
  rectangle "Logical Data Model" as ZM1
}
package "ZACHMAN: Designer-How slot" as Z_DH {
  rectangle "System Function Model" as ZM2
}
ZM1 ..> ZM2 : same row, different interrogative (no flow)

' ============ RIGHT: UAF (framework with relationships) ============
package "UAF: Systems-Resources" as U_SR {
  node "Radar" as U1
  node "Fusion Engine" as U2
}
package "UAF: Operational-Activities" as U_OA {
  usecase "Classify Contact" as U3
}
U1 --> U2 : data flow (needline)
U2 --> U3 : supports activity (needline)
note right of U2 : UAF defines HOW elements relate (needlines, measures)
